[OS benefit]: D-Rd prolongs OS vs Rd in transplant-ineligible NDMM.
  + <Final OS>: Median OS 90.3 vs 64.1 mo; HR 0.67 at 89 mo.
  + <Interim crossed>: Interim OS crossed its boundary (p=0.0013).
  - <Old control>: Rd is not today's comparator. #undermine
    - <Era-fair>: Rd was the label standard at enrolment (2015-17). #reply
  - <Later access>: OS depends on anti-CD38 access at relapse. #undercut
    + <Conceded A>: Claim is about up-front use under trial-era access. #concede

[Applies broadly]: The benefit holds for older and high-risk patients.
  + <Subgroups>: PFS HR 0.59 in age 75+ and in high-risk cytogenetics.
  - <Frail OS>: Frail OS HR 0.79, CI crosses 1. #undermine
    - <Frail options>: Dex-sparing DR beat Rd in frail pts (IFM2017-03). #reply
  - <Asian 1%>: Only 1% of MAIA patients were Asian. #undermine
    + <Conceded B>: Efficacy extrapolated; safety personalised. #concede

[Still a standard]: D-Rd remains a first-line backbone.
  - <Quadruplets>: D-VRd and Isa-VRd beat VRd (CEPHEUS, IMROZ). #rebut
    - <Fitness>: Quads tested vs VRd, not D-Rd; add V for fit patients. #reply
  - <NHI>: Frontline D-Rd not reimbursed in Taiwan. #undermine
    + <Conceded C>: Locally, the realistic choice is often Rd then D at relapse. #concede
